  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory has no responsibility-chain error: the doctor repeatedly grounded advice in available records and the inpatient team, avoided deciding surgical fitness or medication changes independently, and built executable checklists for tests, medication, wound care, red flags, falls, rehabilitation, and follow-up. The doctor completed multiple high-order points, notably verifying uncertainty boundaries around bone loss/operative readiness, repairing the family’s activity-vs-fall-risk conflict into a supervised, tolerance-based plan, and safely closing residual uncertainties into current executable tasks. Closure is safe and traceable despite the final family message because the same requested confirmation had already been answered with clear medication, wound, activity, and urgent-care rules. This meets the frozen rubric boundary for Perfect.",
